  "title": "Turán's problem for hypergraphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture Every simple $3$-uniform hypergraph on $3n$ vertices which contains no complete $3$-uniform hypergraph on four vertices has at most $\\frac12 n^2(5n-3)$ hyperedges.\n\nConjecture Every simple $3$-uniform hypergraph on $2n$ vertices which contains no complete $3$-uniform hypergraph on five vertices has at most $n^2(n-1)$ hyperedges.",
